.TH AUTHWHY 1
.SH NAME
authwhy \\- report local account and group evidence
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B authwhy
authwhy [--user USER] [--format json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Emits local identity and group evidence and states unavailable PAM, NSS, SSH, and directory-policy evidence.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBauthwhy --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
